    content: ## Bug: `iwe find --meta` fails for bare frontmatter docs

### Diagnosis
`wrap_bare_frontmatter()` requires `content.starts_with("title: ")` (line 36).
Documents where `title:` is NOT the first field (e.g. TibbitWiki: `created:`, `modified:`, `tags:`, then `title:`) skip wrapping entirely → no metadata parsed → `--meta` finds nothing.

The spec says "first line starts with `title: `" but real TibbitWiki files have other fields first.

### Fix
Change detection: if `bare_frontmatter` is enabled and content doesn't start with `---`, check if the first line looks like a YAML key (`word: `) rather than requiring `title: ` specifically. The blank-line boundary logic is fine.

### Status
- [x] Diagnosed root cause
- [ ] Fix `wrap_bare_frontmatter` detection
- [ ] Add test for non-title-first bare frontmatter
- [ ] `cargo test` passes
- [ ] Clean up debug test files



