test result: ok. 9 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.01sAll passing. The fix is already applied and tests are green. Here's the summary:

## Root Cause

`wrap_bare_frontmatter()` in `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs` required `content.starts_with("title: ")` — documents where `title:` wasn't the **first** field (e.g. TibbitWiki files with `created:`, `modified:`, `tags:` before `title:`) were never wrapped with `---` fences, so pulldown-cmark never parsed them as metadata blocks. No metadata → `--meta` filtering always returned empty.

The existing tests all used `title:` as the first line, so they passed.

## Fix

Changed the detection from requiring `title: ` as the first line to accepting **any valid YAML key** (`alphanumeric`, `_`, `-` followed by `: `) on the first line. This matches the actual bare frontmatter format used by TibbitWiki and similar systems.

## Files Changed

- **`crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs`** — Broadened `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` detection from `starts_with("title: ")` to a general YAML-key check on the first line
- **`crates/liwe/tests/bare_frontmatter_test.rs`** — Added `reader_detects_bare_non_title_first` test covering the `created:` → `title:` field order case

The `transform_action_with_env_vars` failure is pre-existing (fails on the unmodified commit too).

